    {
      "block_id": "b00001",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Where and When Does IR35 Apply?",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00002",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Buying organisations are reminded of the steps they should take where the IR35 rules apply and where:",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00003",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "individuals are engaged through an intermediary company (typically a Personal Service Company or PSC) under one of the Scottish Government Temporary and Interim Staff Services Framework Agreements;",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00004",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "individuals are engaged through an intermediary company (typically a Personal Service Company or PSC) under one of the Scottish Government Temporary and Interim Staff Services Framework Agreements;",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00005",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "a PSC is engaged directly by a public body; and,",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00006",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "a PSC is engaged directly by a public body; and,",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00007",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "organisations are considering using a non-Scottish Government led Framework Agreement to engage temporary or interim workers.",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00008",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "organisations are considering using a non-Scottish Government led Framework Agreement to engage temporary or interim workers.",
      "ordinal": 8,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00009",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Further Detail",
      "ordinal": 9,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00010",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Scottish Procurement Policy Note (SPPN) 2/2017 provides further information on using the Scottish Government Temporary and Interim Staff Services Framework Agreements and direct engagements of PSCs.",
      "ordinal": 10,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00011",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "HMRC has published guidance online, which includes a tool to check for employments status for tax. Also, the HMRC tool should assist organisations in assessing where IR35 applies to engagements they have with temporary or interim staff.",
      "ordinal": 11,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00012",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "HMRC has published guidance online, which includes a tool to check for employments status for tax. Also, the HMRC tool should assist organisations in assessing where IR35 applies to engagements they have with temporary or interim staff.",
      "ordinal": 12,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00013",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "The buyer’s guide associated with the Scottish Government Temporary and Interim Staff Services framework agreements can be found on the Scottish Procurement website.",
      "ordinal": 13,
      "heading_path": [],
